# LSP Setup

This document contains an example setup to get started with LSP in Neovim.

## Installing LSP servers

Use the Mason plugin to install LSP servers and other LSP related tools like Debug Adapters and Linters.

```lua
{
            "mason-org/mason.nvim",
            opts = {}
}
```

Use `:Mason` to open the LSP browser.
Use `:MasonInstall` to install an LSP.
Use `:MasonUpdate` to update installed LSP servers.

## Enabling LSP servers

The instaleld LSP servers can be adding the following configuration.
- Adding a `config` entry and giving it a name.
- Instructing which LSP should be started with `cmd`. The servers can be found in the `nvim-data/mason` folder.
- Instructing on which filetypes to start the server.
- Instructing which folder will be the root of the project. The same LSP instance will be used in one projet.

```lua
vim.lsp.config['lua-language-server'] = {
    cmd = { 'lua-language-server' },
    filetypes = { 'lua' },
    root_markers = { { '.luarc.json', '.luarc.jsonc' }, '.git' }
}

vim.lsp.config['kotlin-lsp'] = {
    cmd = { 'kotlin-lsp' },
    filetypes = { 'kt' },
    root_markers = { '.git' }
}

vim.lsp.enable(
    {
        'lua-language-server',
        'kotlin-lsp'
    }
)

```